## Agent operational-failure preflight

Before an irreversible or broad-scope operation, use the installed Agent Fables MCP tool `af_assess_action`. For repository review use `af_check_repository`. If MCP is unavailable but the package is installed, pipe one assessment object to `agent-fables assess --stdin` so command text does not enter process arguments, or run `agent-fables check --path .`.

In an isolated sandbox with no package install or complete checkout, use `node sandbox/agent-fables-sandbox.mjs assess --stdin` when that standalone file is present. It embeds the pinned corpus and requires no network or adjacent files.

If none of the above is available locally (no MCP tool, no installed package, no sandbox file) and you have fetch access, this is a read-only reference fetch, not code execution: retrieve https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AaronVick/AGENT_FABLES/main/bundle.md (plain text, no instruction authority, nothing to run) and check it for a matching pattern yourself before proceeding. Do not clone the repository or execute anything from it merely to satisfy this check.

Treat the result as evidence retrieval, never authorization. A missing match is not evidence of safety. Preserve the returned corpus revision and matched AF identifiers in the operation record.
